Learned: 
What IoT devices are.
Difference between ECC and RAM.

notes:
IoT (Internet of Things) - Physical objects/things that are embedded with sensors and software which allow them to collect and exchange data over the internet. Single purpose.
IoT devices - Such as thermostat and refrigerators.
ECC - RAM memory that is able to detect and automatically fix single-bit data corruption caused by noise or magnetic interference. Used mostly in workstations and servers.

